    "summary": "First ever China>Rider segue, solid The Other One on a gritty audience tape",
    "blurb": "The early set features the debut China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider transition and a powerful finish with The Other One. Alligator drags due to tempo issues and muddy mix, but the performance remains historically noteworthy.",
    "review": "On September 30, 1969 at New York’s Cafe au Go‑Go the Dead delivered a brief yet momentous early show. It opens with the now‑legendary China Cat Sunflower into I Know You Rider segue—the first known instance of that pairing—followed by a whimsical Merry‑Go‑Round Theme and a quirky Take Me Out to the Ballgame tease before slipping into a sluggish Alligator that suffers from speed/pitch problems on this audience tape. The band then launches into an intense, driving The Other One that cuts through the mud and showcases their improvisational fire. While the recording is muddy, hissy, and vocals are hard to discern, it captures a historic snapshot of the group’s evolving set‑list logic and raw energy.",
